# Captured engine I/O is a byte oracle: the printouts and decks are compared
# byte-for-byte against what a real engine emits, and their CRLF line endings
# are part of the evidence (see the 2026-08-20 ws4 sitting, where momwire's
# LF-only printout was the reason EZNEC refused the drop-in engine). Never let
# autocrlf normalise them.
scratch/eznec-capture/** -text
scratch/4nec2-capture/** -text
# AK#1705's driving decks are byte-exact copies of the nec-wild originals
# (one is CRLF); keep git from normalising them.
tests/fixtures/sy_knobs_1705/*.nec -text
# AK#1714's driving circuits are byte-exact copies of AC6LA's SimNEC examples
# (both mix CRLF and LF line ends); keep git from normalising them.
tests/fixtures/ssn_dcl_knobs_1714/*.ssn -text
